[{"id":3669686604,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOEFLz887auvlM","user":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]","id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-pull-request-reviewer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR refactors the PreAuthKey system to support tags-only authentication keys without requiring a user, enabling tagged nodes to be created without user ownership. The changes shift from user-based to ID-based operations for the PreAuthKey API.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Refactored PreAuthKey API operations to use ID-based instead of user+key combinations\n- Allow PreAuthKey creation without a user when tags are provided\n- Updated CLI commands to use `--id` parameter for expire/delete operations\n- Added integration tests for tags-only auth key behavior\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 18 out of 18 changed files in this pull request and generated 1 comment.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| proto/headscale/v1/preauthkey.proto | Changed API to use ID-based operations; removed user parameter from list/expire/delete requests |\r\n| hscontrol/grpcv1.go | Simplified API handlers to work with ID-based operations; removed user validation checks |\r\n| hscontrol/state/state.go | Added support for tags-only PreAuthKeys without user ownership in node registration |\r\n| hscontrol/db/preauth_keys.go | Updated database functions to work with IDs and support listing all keys |\r\n| hscontrol/db/users.go | Modified user deletion to handle keys when PreAuthKeys list all keys |\r\n| cmd/headscale/cli/preauthkeys.go | Updated CLI to use ID-based operations with `--id` flags |\r\n| integration/hsic/hsic.go | Added AuthKeyOptions structure to support tags-only auth keys |\r\n| integration/tags_test.go | Added tests for tags-only PreAuthKey registration scenarios |\r\n| integration/cli_test.go | Updated tests to remove user parameter from list operations |\r\n| gen/ | Regenerated protobuf code |\r\n| CHANGELOG.md | Documented breaking API changes |\n</details>\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (2)</summary>\n\n**hscontrol/db/users.go:70**\n* This code deletes ALL preauth keys in the system when deleting a user, not just the keys belonging to that user. Since `ListPreAuthKeys(tx)` now returns all keys system-wide, this will incorrectly delete preauth keys owned by other users or tags-only keys. The loop should filter keys to only delete those where `key.UserID` matches the user being deleted, or a filtered list function should be used.\n```\n\tkeys, err := ListPreAuthKeys(tx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tfor _, key := range keys {\n\t\terr = DestroyPreAuthKey(tx, key.ID)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n**integration/cli_test.go:431**\n* This test still uses the old `--user` flag for the create command. While the flag is now optional according to the PR changes, for consistency with the new behavior where user is optional, consider either removing this parameter or adding a comment explaining why it's still being used in this test case.\n```\n\t\t\t\t\"--user\",\n\t\t\t\t\"1\",\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/juanfont/headscale/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2992#pullrequestreview-3669686604","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2992","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2992#pullrequestreview-3669686604"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2992"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T09:12:27Z","commit_id":"0a5cced5dc28d955d0cdb21761c4b352a4e2c932"},{"id":3670294963,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOEFLz887axEGz","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizati